README.md:327 says:

  "The 76 *List classes ... have not been real classes since the 1.00
   Moose-to-Moo rewrite. Use `IO::K8s::List` to inflate any List-shaped
   payload."

and README.md:400 lists IO::K8s::List as "List-typed inflation (PodList,
ServiceList, ...)". There is no inflation. IO::K8s::List is write-only.

Measured on 4887f658:

  $k8s->json_to_object('{"kind":"PodList","apiVersion":"v1",
                         "metadata":{...},"items":[{...}]}');
  # Cannot resolve Kubernetes GVK: kind 'PodList', apiVersion 'v1'

  $k8s->struct_to_object('+IO::K8s::List', $list_struct);
  # Can't locate object method "_k8s_attr_info" via package
  #   "IO::K8s::List" at lib/IO/K8s.pm line 887.

Both are consistent with the code: IO::K8s::List is hand-written Moo, not
IO::K8s::Resource, so it has no attribute registry for _inflate_struct to
read; it has no FROM_STRUCT, so _struct_to_object_expanded's self-inflating
branch does not fire either; and no *List Kind is in %DEFAULT_RESOURCE_MAP,
so inflate() fails closed on it -- correctly, given karr #39, but there is
nothing behind the failure.

The class has: items (ro, required, untyped ArrayRef), metadata, item_class,
api_version, kind, TO_JSON, to_json. Serialization only.

WHO IS AFFECTED
Not Kubernetes::REST -- verified against the installed 1.107: its
_inflate_list (REST.pm:447-456) decodes the body itself, inflates each item
through struct_to_object, and constructs IO::K8s::List from the results. It
never asks IO::K8s to inflate a List payload, and list() resolves the class
through expand_class first, so it hands a fully-qualified item_class.

Affected is every standalone use: `kubectl get pods -o json` piped into
json_to_object, a stored List-kind manifest, a multi-document apply file
with a `kind: List` wrapper, or anyone following the README sentence above.
That is the single most common response shape of the Kubernetes API and it
cannot be read back.

DECIDE FIRST -- this is a scope question, not a bug fix
  (a) Implement it: give IO::K8s::List a FROM_STRUCT that inflates items by
      their own apiVersion/kind (each item in a real API list response
      carries neither -- the API server omits them inside items -- so the
      item type has to come from the LIST's kind minus the 'List' suffix
      plus its apiVersion, with item_class as an override). Then teach
      inflate() to route a /List$/ kind to IO::K8s::List. Note this reopens
      a resolution path karr #39 deliberately closed, so it must fail closed
      the same way: an unresolvable item GVK is an error, never a silent
      empty list.
  (b) Decide it is out of scope and fix the README, which currently promises
      a feature that does not exist. Then say where the inflation belongs
      (Kubernetes::REST already does it) and add a
      maint/spec-drift-exceptions.yaml note so the decision survives.

(a) is the honest reading of the README and of "unified IO::K8s::List
replaces the 76 classes". (b) is defensible only if the distribution's
position is that it models objects and Kubernetes::REST owns transport.
Whichever is chosen, README.md:327 and :400 must end up true.

Blast radius if (a): touches inflate()'s dispatch, which karr #11/#17/#31/
#32/#39 have all been through. Read t/49_crd_resource_map_gvk.t and
t/40_karr_11_multi_version_dispatch.t before changing it.

Test: t/44_list_api_version.t owns the List apiVersion/kind claims and is
the place for a round-trip -- a real PodList payload in, TO_JSON out,
structurally equal.

Found reviewing the 1.105 *List removal against the current entry points.

